  "rationale": "**Holds.** The prewarm's only acquisition path is `refresh_installation_if_present` -> `symposium_install::refresh_source_if_present`. That returns `Ok(false)` without acquiring anything unless `source_is_cached` finds the source on disk: crates.io cargo needs the `current` pointer and a cached binary for it, `cargo + git` needs the binary in its commit-keyed cache dir (and a known executable name), GitHub needs its cache path, and global cargo is always `false`. An installation with no `source` returns `Ok(())` immediately. `install_commands` run only when a refresh actually ran. `prewarm_hook_sources` calls nothing else that acquires.\n\n**Tests (pass, `cargo test -p symposium-install --lib`):** `refresh_source_if_present_skips_absent_source` (nothing cached -> no refresh, and the binaries dir is not created), `source_is_cached_crates_io_present_and_absent`, `source_is_cached_cargo_git_probes_commit_keyed_dir`, `source_is_cached_global_is_never_managed`. There is no end-to-end `SessionStart` test of this; the wiring from `prewarm_hook_sources` is judged from code.\n",
  "requirement": "The `SessionStart` source refresh MUST NOT install a plugin hook source that was never installed."
}
